'''Nippet''' was an [[Ewok]] [[Reproduction|born]] in [[3 BBY]] as daughter of [[Zephee]] of the [[Bright Tree tribe]] on the [[moon]] of [[Endor]]. As the youngest member of the tribe, Nippet captivated those around her and explored the forest with help from her [[Parent|mother]].

In [[4 ABY]], Nippet hid in fear when the [[3PO-series protocol droid|protocol droid]] [[C-3PO]] was [[Telekinesis|raised into the air]] above the [[Bright Tree Village]] center by the [[Jedi]] [[Luke Skywalker]] in an attempt to scare the Ewoks into freeing Skywalker and his [[Heroes of Yavin|companions]] from captivity. The [[wokling]] later listened to C-3PO tell stories of Skywalker's adventures and squeaked in terror when the [[Protocol droid|droid]] described the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]].

==Biography==
===Wonderful wokling===
[[File:Woklings_AEYNTK.jpg|thumb|right|300px|alt=Four woklings sit together with Nippet at the center.|Nippet, daughter of Zephee, was one of the woklings of Bright Tree Village.]]
Nippet was an [[Ewok]] [[Gender|female]] [[Reproduction|born]] in [[3 BBY]] on<ref name="Cosbaby" /> the [[forest]] [[moon]]<ref name="Beware" /> [[Endor]]. She and her [[Parent|mother]], [[Zephee]],<ref name="Cosbaby" /> were part of the [[Bright Tree tribe]] that lived in [[Bright Tree Village]] on Endor.<ref name="Beware" /> Zephee helped Nippet learn and explore their forest home with a gentle touch and warm smile, teaching her daughter the true essence of being an Ewok.<ref name="Zephee">{{Instagram|username=cosbaby|url=p/DITPYMxvyie/?img_index=1|name=[[Hot Toys|Cosbaby By Hot Toys]]|date=2025-04-11|quote=The mother figure of the Ewoks, Zephee, embodies a nurturing and compassionate spirit and cares deeply for everyone around her. She has a unique talent for listening, making each Ewok feel valued and understood. Her gentle guidance fosters a strong sense of community and encourages care for others. With her gentle touch and warm smile, she helps her daughter, Baby Nippet (a Wokling), learn and explore their beautiful forest, teaching her the true essence of being an Ewok. #HotToysCollectibles #Cosbaby #Cosbi #CosbiPlushKeychain #StarWars #Lucasfilm #Ewok #Zephee|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/lfI74|archivefile=File:Cosbaby-Zephee-Instagram.png}}</ref> Nippet also had a sister and when<ref name="FC" /> the [[Galactic Empire]] began constructing the [[DS-2 Death Star II Mobile Battle Station|Death Star II]] [[superweapon]] over Endor,<ref name="Beware" /> Zephee worried what terrible things its completion would mean for her tribe and [[Youngling|children]].<ref name="FC" />

===Scary stories===
{{Quote|Eek!|Nippet squeaks at C-3PO's re-enactment of Darth Vader|audio=Nippet-EEK.flac|<ref name="Beware" />}}
In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Date">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas: Updated Edition]]'' dates the events of {{Film|VI}} to [[4 ABY]].</ref> Nippet was just a small<ref name="Beware" /> [[wokling]]<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> when a [[scout]]ing party led by the Ewok [[Teebo]]<ref name="USW">''[[Ultimate Star Wars, New Edition]]''</ref> returned with a [[Heroes of Yavin|group]] of [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|rebels]] that had been caught in one of the tribe's net traps. The Ewoks of the village had mistaken one of the captives, the [[3PO-series protocol droid|protocol droid]] [[C-3PO]], for the [[deity]]<ref name="ROTJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> known as the [[Golden One]]<ref name="Vader">[[Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle 4|''Star Wars Adventures: Tales from Vader's Castle'' 4]]</ref> and so seated him on a [[throne]] in the village center,<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> where Nippet was seated in a basket. As Nippet watched the proceedings,<ref name="ROTJ" /> Zephee<ref name="AD">{{Film|VI}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> stroked the wokling's head.<ref name="ROTJ" />

[[File:NippetStories.png|thumb|left|300px|alt=A cluster of Ewoks stand in a darkened hut listening to stories. On the right, one holds Nippet and on the left stands Widdle Warrick.|Nippet listened to C-3PO tell stories.]]
The tribe then prepared to sacrifice the captives in C-3PO's honor, placing the [[human]]s [[Han Solo]] and [[Luke Skywalker]] over cooking [[fire]]s to be made part of a grand banquet for the [[Protocol droid|droid]]. Skywalker then had C-3PO tell the Ewoks to spare his companions, warning that he would otherwise become angry. When the Ewoks ignored the threat, Skywalker used [[the Force]] to [[Telekinesis|lift]] the [[droid]] into the [[Atmosphere|air]], causing the Ewoks present to panic.<ref name="ROTJ" />

As C-3PO floated above the platform, Nippet squealed in terror and hid within the basket. After the Ewoks had freed the captives, Nippet was among the residents of the village that gathered<ref name="ROTJ" /> in [[Chief]] [[Chirpa]]'s hut<ref name="CL" /> with their new allies to listen to C-3PO tell stories of Skywalker's various adventures in [[Galactic Civil War|fighting]] the Empire. During the storytelling, Nippet was held in the [[Limb|arms]] of a [[Color|brown]] [[Hair|furred]] Ewok who stood next to<ref name="ROTJ" /> [[Widdle Warrick]].<ref name="Disney">''[[Disney Infinity 3.0]]''</ref> After the droid introduced the [[Dark Lord of the Sith|Sith Lord]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and recreated the sound of his [[Darth Vader's armor|breathing]], Nippet let out a yelp of terror.<ref name="Beware" /> Once the story was finished, Chirpa made the former captives into members of the tribe and agreed to help the rebels in their [[Battle of Endor|fight]] against the Empire.<ref name="ROTJ" />

==Personality and traits==
As a wokling, Nippet was innocent and fun-loving, embodying a sense of wonder and innocence that captivated all those around her as her tribe's favorite wokling while she was the youngest Ewok in the group. She explored her homeworld's lush forests with wide-eyed curiosity and discovered the beauty of its environment as well as the joys of friendship, bringing joy and lightness to the group with her playful nature and reminding others of the true essence of love and happiness.<ref name="Cosbaby" />

Nippet was scared by the apparent demonstration of C-3PO's divine powers<ref name="ROTJ" /> and the droid's description of [[Darth]] Vader but was fascinated by the adventure, heroism, and sound effects in C-3PO's story.<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> The wokling had chestnut brown and white fur, black [[eye]]s, and light skin. As a wokling she stood one [[foot]] (thirty [[centimeter]]s) tall.<ref name="Cosbaby" /> By the time of the Battle of Endor,<ref name="ROTJ" /> Nippet could not yet [[Language|speak]] beyond babbling.<ref name="Cosbaby" />

==Behind the scenes==
[[File:NippetPuppet.jpg|thumb|right|300px|alt=With slightly matted fur and some wear, the Nippet puppet sites beside a ruler.|The Nippet puppet was auctioned in 2019.]]
Nippet first appeared in the [[1983]] [[original trilogy]] film, [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']].<ref name="ROTJ" /> The wokling was portrayed via puppet with a sheet foam body, plastic eyes, and a foam latex face, ears, and hands, all covered in faux fur. In the bottom of the puppet there is an opening for a puppeteer's hand, and a puppeteering wire in the wrists and neck allows for movement. The dimensions when sitting are 53.5 centimeters by 35.75 centimeters by 38 centimeters (21 inches by 14 inches by 15 inches).<ref name="Auction">{{WebCite|url=https://ukm.propstoreauction.com/m/lot-details/index/catalog/169/lot/47401|text=Lot #777 - STAR WARS: RETURN OF THE JEDI (1983) - Child Ewok Puppet|work=[https://ukm.propstoreauction.com ukm.propstoreauction.com]|archivedate=20210317132325}}</ref>

Puppeteer [[Mike Quinn]] modified the inside of the puppet's head with a thumb grip and finger grip made from gaffer tape and glued inside the mouth so that the lips could be manipulated.<ref name="YouTube">{{YouTube|video=OByNvSilKtw|text=Adam Savage Meets an Original Star Wars Ewok Puppet!|channel=@tested|name=Adam Savage’s Tested|date=2024-12-27}} {{C|Comment by [[Mike Quinn]]: "I was the puppeteer for this exact same puppet. This was the one held by the mother Ewok, performed by Katie Purvis, daughter of the late, great Jack Purvis (IYKYK). I showed up on set and was presented with what was basically a cast foam shell with the fur on it. But the interior of the head wasn’t fitted out as a puppet. All that was inside was a wire going between the two ears. You can actually see this when they show inside the head. It’s still there. So I quickly made up a thumb grip and finger grip from gaffer tape and glued them both inside the mouth. That way I could get it to move a little, as though he was sucking or pursing his lips. I used the wire between the ears to help subtly squish the head by pulling down on it with one of my fingers, to give the illusion of his cheeks flexing. You can also at see all that going on if you look closely in the final movie. I don’t remember the wires coming out of the arms but they were probably used to pull them back. I glued the same type of grips into Nippet, the brown Ewok too. To perform him I had to lay flat on my back to keep out of shot. Surprising and surreal to see it all these decades later. Thanks for showing this. I’d like to meet this little guy again. 😎"}} {{C|[[:File:MikeQuinn-Nippet-YouTube.png|screenshot]]}}</ref> As of [[2019]], when the puppet was sold for £22,500 at auction, the prop had some fading to the paint throughout, the rubber was fragile from age, and there was rusting to the puppeteering wire.<ref name="Auction" /> The Ewok village scenes were filmed between [[January 18]] and [[February 2]], [[1982]] on Stage 3 at [[Elstree Studios]].<ref name="MakingOf">''[[The Making of Star Wars: Return of the Jedi]]''</ref>

In the new ''[[Star Wars]]'' [[canon]], the wokling was first named in ''[[Return of the Jedi: Beware the Power of the Dark Side!]]'', a [[2015]] adaptation of ''Return of the Jedi'' written by [[Tom Angleberger]]. The name was misspelled as "Nippett" in the adaptation,<ref name="Beware" /> but the correct spelling was later used in the [[2017]] reference book ''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''.<ref name="Geektionary" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, an [[Ewok/Legends|Ewok]] named [[Nippet/Legends|Nippet]] first appeared in the [[1984]] storybook ''[[The Baby Ewoks' Picnic Surprise]]'', which was written by [[Melinda Luke]].<ref name="Picnic">''[[The Baby Ewoks' Picnic Surprise]]''</ref> The wokling seen in ''Return of the Jedi'' was established to be Nippet by an action figure of the character released as part of the ''[[Star Wars: The Legacy Collection]]'' toy line by [[Hasbro]] in [[2008]].<ref name="Hasbro">{{HasbroCite|set=Star Wars: The Legacy Collection|pack=#04: Leektar & Nippet|altlink=https://www.rebelscum.com/tlc04ewoks.asp}}</ref>

